SUMARR - crunch a whole numeric array at native speed.

Language features
  - SEED_EXPORT; the payoff case for native code
  - a direct, zero-copy pointer into a BASIC array's storage

Try it
  DIM A(1000) : ... fill A() ...
    SEED h%, "SUMARR.SED" : PRINT CALL(h%, "A")

Build it on the machine
  grow sumarr          # -> build/SUMARR.SED
It is also prebuilt in /SEED as SUMARR.SED, ready to use.

